    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0149" n="23" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg23"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760c.6215/414</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Poland</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Pearson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic">June 5,
                        1925</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 123</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: There is enclosed herewith for your
                    confidential information a copy of a Memorandum left by the Polish Minister on
                    May 28, <pb facs="0150" n="24" xml:id="pg24"/> 1925. Upon being apprised of the
                    contents of the Memorandum I drew the Minister’s attention to the fact that the
                    United States could not in any way associate itself with a Security Pact<anchor
                        n="36" xml:id="d29-f1"/> and must maintain an entirely neutral position with
                    regard to any boundary disputes arising in connection therewith. The Polish
                    Minister stated that he understood the situation perfectly.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank B. Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d29-a1.xml" xpointer="d29-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d29-f1" n="36" xml:id="d29-f1-content">
                <p>For statement on the work of the Locarno Conference, see the President’s message
                    to Congress, December 8, <ref target="#pgVII">p. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >vii</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
